    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0391" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v34/pg361"/>

                <head>195. Telegram From the Embassy in the United Kingdom to the Department of
                        State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d195-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>London</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1966-11-22T18:25:00+00:00">November 22, 1966,
                        1825Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>4274. Subject: Iranian Oil. During conversations in London yesterday, Under
                    Secretary Rostow stressed importance our parallel efforts to ensure success of
                    oil talks this week in Iran.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d195-f2"/> While we did not
                    get as far as British Government did with oil companies, we had made clear both
                    to GOI and to American oil companies our sense of the sensitivity of situation
                    and our hope they would reach a reasonable compromise acknowledging the rightful
                    interests of both sides. FonMin Brown urged separate American approach to Aramco
                    with respect both to present negotiations and possible future Aramco
                    transactions with Saudi Arabia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold"> Bruce </hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d195-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d195-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives and Records Administration, RG 59, Records of the
                    Department of State, Central Files, 1964–66, PET 6 IRAN. Secret. Repeated to
                    Tehran and Jidda.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d195-f2" n="2" xml:id="d195-f2-content">
                <p>On November 26 Ambassador Meyer reported in telegram 2298 from Tehran that the
                    Consortium team had tentatively completed its negotiations with the Iranians.
                    (Ibid., PET 6 IRAN)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
